<title>USA: MBIA qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance. [CORRECTED 15:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance. [CORRECTED 15:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. said on Monday it qualified for bond insurance the following five municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Bronson CSD, Mich., $1.65 million building and site.</p>
<p>--Elk River, Minn., $1.165 million GO improvement.</p>
<p>--Inver Grove Heights, Minn., $5.25 million GO water revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--LaCrescent, Minn., $1.28 million GO improvement.</p>
<p>--Hopkins County, Texas, $1.4 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
<p>(Correcting in title and first paragraph the number qualified for bond insurance from six to five and removing San Marco's, Texas.)</p>
